  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluation of the Regional Programme on Local Democracy in the Western Balkans (ReLOaD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The main objectives of this evaluation are to provide the relevant services of the European Union, the interested stakeholders and the wider public with:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;an overall independent assessment of the performance of ReLOaD (including both phases, implemented in the period 2017-2020 and 2021-2024, respectively)&lt;em&gt;,&lt;/em&gt; paying particular attention to its different levels of results measured against its expected objectives; and the reasons underpinning such results&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;bullet&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;key lessons learned, conclusions and related recommendations in order to improve current and future interventions.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;To that end, the evaluation will be tailored to engage relevant stakeholders (local governments, civil society, communities, individuals, etc.), to enable their feedback and contribution to overall participatory assessment of the ReLOaD&#xbf;s performance, to reflect on the ReLOaD&#xbf;s work and identify signals of transformational change in the thematic areas addressed by the Action. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Participation of the stakeholders will help the evaluation generate collective insights and distil key lessons learned from the implementation of ReLOaD so far &#xbf; including in relation to important cross-cutting issues, such as gender equality, leaving no one behind - and propose strategic recommendations for addressing or reinforcing these in the future work in the area of concern.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
